From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odonnellmatt <odonnellmatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:52:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/pad: on a phone, the layout editor's panel is a compact
 bar

The layout editor's panel was made for the iPad: a card up to 400 points
wide in the middle of the screen. On a phone held sideways (375 to 440
points tall) it covers most of the controls being arranged, and the two-way
choice's German and French titles have 1 to 2 points to spare at 375
points.

On a phone (DM_PAD_EDIT_COMPACT unset and an iPhone, or =1 on any device;
=0 keeps the card) DmPadEditPanel is a compact bar (DmPadEditor.h, "The
compact bar"):

- It holds the chosen group's name, its - and + and size, Both sides
  together | Each side on its own, Cancel and Done, and a last button (...)
  that shows the rest below them: All controls with its slider, Save for
  (in the shell) and Reset to default. The chosen group's slider gives way
  to - and +; VoiceOver's element for each group still takes swipes up and
  down. Choosing a group on the gamepad folds the rest away again.
- Its rows follow the width (DmPadEditing.h's dm_pad_compact_rows):
  everything on one row where it fits (a 6.9-inch phone held sideways in
  English), the choice on a row of its own where not (every phone held
  sideways in German and French), and Cancel and Done on a third row on a
  phone held upright. The row count takes Cancel and Done at their 44-point
  floor and gives the choice 8 points of room, so a short label ("OK")
  never lets the choice's titles be squeezed.
- Every control on it is at least 44 points tall and wide: - and +, the
  button for the rest, the choice, Save for, the All controls slider,
  Cancel, Done (whatever the length of its label) and Reset to default.
- Where it sits (dm_pad_dock_edge, DmGamepad.m's editDock): across the safe
  area's middle, 4 points from its top or bottom edge, so it keeps off the
  sensor housing and the home indicator. With nothing chosen, on the edge
  where it covers the fewest groups; a group just chosen sends it to the
  edge away from it (with its mirror image while the two move together,
  and the room for its tag); a chosen group dragged under it sends it to
  the other edge, animated unless Reduce Motion is on. A drag on the
  group's name moves it to the other edge too. A bar taller than the safe
  area keeps to the top, Cancel and Done in its first rows.
- "No room there" shows on a dark pill just outside the bar, on the side
  away from its edge, so it takes no room in the bar.

The card on an iPad is unchanged: the same rows, the same places (placeIn:
and keepIn: only return early for the bar). The bar is measured again only
when the safe area's width or the rest shown changes; while a group moves
it only picks its edge (arithmetic on a few rectangles). No new words: the
bar uses DM_PAD_EDIT_TEXT's 27 lines.

Docs: settings.md, env_switches.tsv (DM_PAD_EDIT_COMPACT).

Checked here (Linux, no Apple SDK): pad_groups_check.m's check_compact_bar
(the rows on an iPhone SE, 17 and 17 Pro Max screen held sideways and
upright in English, German, French and Japanese with estimated title
widths: never three rows sideways, always three upright; on those screens
sideways, 2D and 3D, no group just chosen, with its mirror image, is under
the bar, and every one dragged under it sends it to the other edge; a bar
taller than the safe area keeps to the top), through test_pad_geometry.py
(clang -Wall -Werror) and under gcc ASan and UBSan; the identity dump
(unchanged); env_switches.py --check, test_docs.py; DmPadEditor.m and
DmGamepad.m through clang -fsyntax-only against declaration stubs.

Run on a Mac, on the author's own tree (this series' feature code on
another base) with the whole series applied: Xcode built it; the next
change's DuoEditorShotTests drove the bar, and the editor's seven harness
cases passed, on Simulators of an iPhone SE (3rd generation), an iPhone 17
and an iPhone 17 Pro Max, held sideways and upright, in English, German and
French (an 11-inch iPad shows the card, also passed). An earlier run there
found Done 38.5 points wide in French and the choice's titles 4.7 points
short on the Pro Max; the 44-point floor and the row count above fix both,
and the run after them passed. Not run: a real iPhone.

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on 0020 and 0040: the seedds/nxnative pull request follows once they are upstream]
Reason: on a phone the layout editor's panel is a compact bar at the top or bottom of the safe area, so it leaves the controls being arranged in view
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1397 (the feature issue, to be opened before the pull request)

