+// ---- The compact bar (a phone) ----
+// On a phone the card would hide the controls being arranged, held sideways most of all. The bar keeps to one edge of the safe area instead (clear of
+// the sensor housing and the home indicator), as narrow as its rows: the chosen group's name, its − and + and size, the two-way choice, Cancel and
+// Done, and a button that shows the rest below them (All controls, Save for, Reset to default). Its rows follow the width: all on one row where they
+// fit (DmPadEditing.h's dm_pad_compact_rows), the choice on a row of its own below the name where not, and Cancel and Done on a third row on a phone
+// held upright. Every control is at least 44 points tall and wide. It docks to the top or the bottom edge, away from the chosen group (and its
+// mirror image when they move together), and moves to the other edge when that group comes under it (dm_pad_dock_edge); the player may also drag it
+// by the group's name to the other edge. A message ("No room there") shows just outside it, on the side away from the edge.
+@property (nonatomic, readonly) BOOL compact;
+@property (nonatomic, readonly) int dockEdge;   // 0 the top, 1 the bottom (-1 before the first dockIn:)
+@property (nonatomic, readonly) int compactRows;   // 1 to 3 (dm_pad_compact_rows), 0 for the card
+@property (nonatomic) BOOL expanded;   // the rest shown below (the button's action, or a test)
+// The bar's size and place in the safe area: group is the chosen group (-1 none), chosen the rectangle it and the groups that move with it cover
+// (CGRectNull for none), rects the other groups'. A group newly chosen puts the bar on the edge away from it.
+- (void)dockIn:(CGRect)safe group:(int)group chosen:(CGRect)chosen avoiding:(NSArray<NSValue *> *)rects;
 @end
 
 NS_ASSUME_NONNULL_END
